# Where the Modern Warfare 4 multiplayer weapon catalog comes from

Everything here was read on **2026-10-24**, the day after launch (2026-10-23).
`catalog.json` lists every weapon a player can put in a Modern Warfare 4
multiplayer loadout at launch, plus three names the HUD showed in gameplay
video that are not launch weapons of their own. **Held for the owner's review**
(`review` in catalog.json, D132): nothing of it reaches a Core's AI Scripts
until he deletes that line.

**Pictures: none.** Every `image` is `null` (owner, 2026-10-24: leave pictures
out; the app falls back to the class symbol). A picture added later follows
D116: Activision's own, from callofduty.com or imgs.callofduty.com, with a row
in a Pictures table here.

## The list

- **Activision, "Ready for Launch: All Modern Warfare 4 Operators, Weapons,
  Equipment, and Multiplayer Create-a-Class Features"**
  ([blog](https://www.callofduty.com/blog/2026/10/call-of-duty-modern-warfare-4-launch-multiplayer-operators-weapons-equipment-create-a-class)),
  read 2026-10-24: **33 weapons**, 24 primary, 8 secondary, 1 melee, under the
  class headings Assault Rifles (8), Submachine Guns (5), Shotguns (2), Light
  Machine Guns (3), Marksman Rifles (3), Sniper Rifles (3), Pistols (4),
  Launchers (4), Melee Weapon (1). Every name and class in the catalog is that
  page's, spelt as it spells them in the weapon cards:
  `Signal 50` (no dot), `PM-40 Anvil`, `Wz.55 Striga`, `SANG 9mm`, `FiNN LMG`.
  Gfinity Esports and Dexerto's MW4 wiki list the same 33 in the same classes.
- **Fire modes:** `burst` for the Hyeon Burst (by name, 375 RPM) and the Krait
  P68 (the blog gives its rate in BPM, bursts a minute). Others are left out.
- **Not a weapon of its own:**
  - `smgs.iso_trace`: the ISO Nightshade's **Apex Attachment** (the blog's
    card: "Apex Attachment: ISO Trace"); the HUD prints "ISO Trace" while it
    is fitted. Every launch gun has one (Han X20 Skybreaker, M4 Hurricane,
    Patriot XMR Volt, Kastov ARC, ...); only ISO Trace has been SEEN on the
    HUD, so only it is listed. If the others also rename the HUD, they are
    added the same way when a frame shows one.
  - `lethal.zip_gun`: lethal equipment (unlocked at Player Level 17); its name
    was seen once on the HUD at a swap.
  - `unconfirmed.volt_edge`: seen on the HUD in an Oris 8.6 gameplay video;
    on no Activision page. Class unknown.

## The HUD's spellings

The gun-name reader (`recognition.json`, D411 route, taught on public
gameplay video: ZeroStick Model Library, Call of Duty/Modern Warfare 4)
reads the HUD's own spellings. `names.hud` records `Signal 50`,
`PM-40 Anvil` and `Wz.55 Striga`; since Activision's list spells them the
same way, the catalog names now match and the entries are kept as the
record of what the HUD prints.

## Ids

Re-made on 2026-10-24 from the class groups (`<group>.<slug>`), replacing the
first draft's single `weapons.` group: the draft never shipped (it carried no
classes and the app held it), so no config or taught picture names an old id.
From now on the README's rule holds: an id never changes.

## Update the list

New weapons arrive with Season 1 (expected 2026-11-06, when Warzone moves onto
Modern Warfare 4): read that season's Modern Warfare 4 patch notes at
https://www.callofduty.com/patchnotes, add each weapon at the end of its group,
and check its name on the HUD (a new letter needs the reader re-taught).
